		{
			"id": "eXKDQsaQnsaBRFfHT",
			"description": "Refractor Field",
			"local_notes": "Shield 20 SP. Recharge: after 2 seconds without taking damage, regains 5 SP per second. Ranged attacks only: melee blows and thrown objects pass through at walking speed. A faint shimmer surrounds the wearer while active (-1 to Holdout, Stealth in darkness -1).\n\nLore: The personal field most associated with Inquisitors, Rogue Traders and senior Imperial agents in Black Library fiction (Eisenhorn and Ravenor among others) and the Dark Heresy and Rogue Trader lines: a shimmering field that scatters incoming fire. Shown as good against a stream of small-arms fire and poor against one heavy hit.\n\nDesign: Small pool, fastest recharge of the Imperial fields, which reproduces the lore: it eats a lasgun hit (avg 14) and is back to full two or three seconds after the shooting pauses, but a single plasma bolt (avg 42) goes straight through. Ranged-only follows the fiction of fields that stop fast projectiles but not slow objects.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "8000",
			"base_weight": "2 lb",
			"uses": 20,
			"max_uses": 20,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eCtxYN74qNBPPLwzu",
			"description": "Rosarius",
			"local_notes": "Shield 30 SP. Recharge: after 3 seconds without taking damage, regains 5 SP per second. Blocks ranged and melee attacks. Worn as an amulet; the field is invisible until struck.\n\nLore: Protection for Ministorum priests, Confessors and Canonesses who fight without full Sororitas plate. Ecclesiarchy background presents it as a blessed relic as much as a device: the faithful credit the Emperor's favour when it holds.\n\nDesign: Two lasgun hits or one bolter round (avg 21) are absorbed; plasma or heavier weapons break through. Ranked below the conversion field and iron halo, matching its role as the field for mortal clergy rather than Astartes officers.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Ecclesiarchy"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "6000",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"uses": 30,
			"max_uses": 30,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eHkkScx8S5hdnk6zC",
			"description": "Conversion Field",
			"local_notes": "Shield 40 SP. Recharge: after 3 seconds without taking damage, regains 5 SP per second. Blocks ranged and melee attacks. Flash: any single hit that removes 10+ SP converts into a burst of light; everyone within 5 yards facing the wearer (not the wearer) rolls HT or is blinded for 1d seconds. Photo-visors and auto-senses negate the flash.\n\nLore: Signature protection of high-ranking Inquisitors and Rogue Traders in Black Library fiction: it turns a chainsword stroke or a point-blank shot into a blinding flare. A rare relic rather than standard Imperial manufacture.\n\nDesign: Absorbs a plasma bolt (avg 42) about half the time, a bolter round easily, and stops nearly any hand weapon wielded by an unaugmented human. The flash is its defining lore trait and makes heavy hits on the wearer dangerous to bystanders.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "1",
			"base_value": "25000",
			"base_weight": "3 lb",
			"uses": 40,
			"max_uses": 40,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eJUTEW1irNlvgX2qX",
			"description": "Iron Halo",
			"local_notes": "Shield 60 SP. Recharge: after 3 seconds without taking damage, regains 10 SP per second. Blocks ranged and melee attacks. Mounted on the backpack of Astartes power armour; needs the armour's power supply.\n\nLore: A relic field worn by Chaplains, Captains and Chapter Masters, per Codex: Space Marines background and Black Library fiction. An honour as well as protection: a Marine is granted one, not issued it.\n\nDesign: Holds against a plasma bolt and most power-weapon blows (a power fist averages ~20) and recovers quickly, so an Astartes hero can walk through small-arms fire in the fiction. A lascannon (avg 112) still breaks it and continues into the armour.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "20000",
			"base_weight": "2 lb",
			"uses": 60,
			"max_uses": 60,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eyjya3iMPBKNN45je",
			"description": "Storm Shield (Field Component)",
			"local_notes": "Shield 80 SP. Recharge: after 2 seconds without taking damage, regains 10 SP per second. Covers only attacks from the front and the shield-arm side (the arcs a shield covers); attacks from behind or the off side bypass it. The physical shield's Defense Bonus and melee stats are on the Storm Shield entry in Melee Weapons.\n\nLore: Astartes and Terminator storm shields pair a solid shield with a kinetic dispersion field, shown in Codex: Space Marines background and Black Library fiction shrugging off blows that would kill a Marine, including the occasional lascannon or plasma hit.\n\nDesign: Largest pool of any personal field, limited to its arc. Plasma (avg 42) is stopped outright; a lascannon (8dx4, avg 112) is stopped only when it rolls 80 or less (8d of 20 or less, about 5% of shots), matching \"occasionally\" in the fiction.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Energy Shield",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Astartes"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "0",
			"base_value": "15000",
			"base_weight": "4 lb",
			"uses": 80,
			"max_uses": 80,
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "eUSWyZtxjHHQ3GXF5",
			"description": "Displacer Field",
			"local_notes": "Not a shield: it has no Shield Points. When the wearer would take damage that penetrates their worn armour, the GM may rule that the field instead teleports them 2d yards in a random direction (as the Teleport advantage, B90), taking no damage from that attack — treat this as usable a limited number of times before the field needs to recharge (recommended: once per few seconds of combat, i.e. about once per turn at most), and note the risk of teleporting into solid matter, off a ledge, or into a worse position is a real one the GM should apply per the Teleport rules.\n\nLore: Displacer fields are archeotech/xenos-derived teleportation wards, most associated in the fiction with Aeldari (Eldar) Farseers and Autarchs, but occasionally captured, reverse- engineered, or gifted relics carried by high-ranking Inquisitors or Rogue Traders in Black Library fiction and Rogue Trader-line background — rather than blocking a killing blow, the wearer simply isn't where the blow lands anymore.\n\nDesign: Deliberately not modelled as DR at all, since the lore mechanic is avoidance rather than resistance: this uses GURPS's existing Teleport advantage (B90) as its design basis rather than any force-field or armour catalogue entry, triggered defensively instead of at will. Marked as TL12^-equivalent xenotech in spirit (warp-adjacent teleportation, per framework.md's \"Warp-dependent\" category) even though it's issued as an Imperial-held relic rather than built by the Imperium; cost and LC reflect extreme rarity and the Inquisition's wariness of xenotech in mortal hands.",
			"tags": [
				"Force Field",
				"Imperium",
				"Inquisition"
			],
			"tech_level": "12",
			"legality_class": "1",
